# ── ⚠️⚠️ A SECOND LOCK, BECAUSE THE FIRST ONE IS ONE CARELESS LINE THICK ─────
#
# `package.json`'s `files` allowlist is what decides the tarball, and it is
# correct today — `npm pack --dry-run` on 2026-08-20 shipped 364 files, all of
# them .mjs / .md / .json plus LICENSE, with nothing sensitive among them.
#
# The reason this file exists anyway: **the repo root currently holds
# `.env.local`**, alongside a dozen scratch captures left by shakedown runs
# (`f.err`, `h.out`, `ws5.out`, `u22.err`, …). None of them ship, for exactly
# one reason — nobody has added a root glob to `files`. The day somebody
# writes `"files": ["*.md", ...]` to pick up a new document, a live key goes to
# the public registry, and `npm unpublish` does not un-leak a credential.
#
# ⭐ npm applies these patterns AFTER the allowlist and INSIDE the directories
# it copies, which is the case an allowlist cannot cover at all: a `lib/.env`
# or a `test/fixtures/token.json` needs no change to `files` to ship.
#
# ⚠️⚠️ THIS BLOCK SAID "THIS FILE MUST NEVER LIST `test/` — shipping the suite is
# deliberate", AND IT WAS DESCRIBING A WORLD THAT NO LONGER EXISTED.
#
# `test/` was dropped from `package.json`'s `files` allowlist, so the suite has
# not shipped for weeks. This note went on asserting the opposite, and so did
# `ENTERPRISE.md`, which told buyers to run `npm test` inside the installed
# package — a command that fails on a directory that isn't there.
#
# ⭐ THE CURRENT POSITION, DECIDED 2026-08-25: the tests are NOT published, and
# the reason is not size. The suite is where this project's engineering argument
# is written down — incidents, measurements, what broke and what it cost. That is
# our working record, and we do not publish our working record.
#
# ⚠️ SO THIS FILE STILL MUST NOT LIST `test/` — but for the opposite reason to
# the one recorded here before. Listing it changes nothing today (the allowlist
# already excludes it); the trap is the reverse move, adding `test/` back to
# `files` to "restore the audit story". The audit story does not need it: zero
# dependencies means the shipped source IS the whole audit.
#
# ⚠️ `scripts/test.mjs` still treats a missing `test/` as a hard failure, which is
# correct for a repo checkout and is why this must never be the only place the
# question is answered. Enforced by `test/publish-readiness.test.mjs`.

# Credentials and anything shaped like one
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
.npmrc

# Scratch captures from debugging runs — the repo root is full of these
*.err
*.out
*.log

# Build artefacts and local state, none of which a consumer can use
dist/
*.tgz
*.tar.gz
*.zip
.acuvo/
.playwright-mcp/
.github/

# Benchmarks: a 52 MB node tarball cache and results that go stale and then
# read as claims. `bench/` is not in the allowlist either.
bench/
results/
